# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else"), ch. 8 ("A new place's first value": the query answers at the build, by the element as built, its field reading the late result), Type System ch. 2 ("Bundles and sparse tuples": the plain part is read once, the push moves the `$` part) and ruling TC: loud gives 10, so the port is "port 10", answered ((7, "up")), its label 1 and the arm's label 2; soft gives 20 and builds nothing in its arm. Never run: prismc refuses the program.
test loud

tick 0
  added:
    0: Pad.Port(name="port 10")
    1: Ui.Label(text="7 up of 10")
    2: Ui.Label(text="x")

tick 1
  in:
    Pad.Port(name="port 10") = ((7, "down"))
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="7 down of 10")

test soft

tick 0
  added:
    0: Pad.Port(name="port 20")
    1: Ui.Label(text="8 up of 20")
